WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.370
BETH: Sensory overload happens when there
is more input from the five senses than

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:07.279
a brain can sort through and process.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:11.549
These could be; multiple
conversations, flashing overhead

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.079
lights, lots of music or loud noise.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:18.939
In most people the brain prioritises
what sensory information to focus

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:23.220
on, but with individuals in autism
this is not straightforward.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:27.470
JOE: Individuals with autism may find
this more of a problem because they may

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:32.519
suffer from hypersensitivity and therefore
things that might not normally cause

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:35.159
sensory overload can seem much worse.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:39.620
Their brain focusses on something
such as a buzzing sound and sends

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:41.019
a message to get away from it.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.790
The body then starts to panic,
and a chain reaction can start.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:50.230
Sensory overload in people with autism
can mean focusing on the smallest most

00:00:50.299 --> 00:00:53.070
insignificant thing over other things.

00:00:53.799 --> 00:00:58.120
It may be flashing lights,
a fluffy carpet, marks on a

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.970
wall, or even a strong smell.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:05.040
BETH: Symptoms of sensory overload
may vary but some common ones include

00:01:05.179 --> 00:01:10.130
difficulty focusing, extreme irritability
or restlessness and discomfort.

00:01:10.719 --> 00:01:13.860
An individual may need to cover
their eyes or ears to shield

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:15.790
themselves from any sensory input.

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:20.390
They may become agitated and stressed
about their surrounding and their

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:23.110
sensitivity to other things may increase.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:28.500
Eventually sensory overload can
cause extreme stress and anxiety,

00:01:28.809 --> 00:01:33.380
physical pain and distressed behaviour
which may develop into a meltdown.

